Converbum finale|<uig rom="oror-a">ᠣᠷᠣᠷ ᠠ</uig>|<uig rom="irer-e">ᠢᠷᠡᠷ ᠡ</uig>|<uig rom="odur-a">ᠣᠳᠤᠷ ᠠ</uig>|<uig rom="öggür-e">ᠥᠭᠭᠦᠷ ᠡ</uig></tbl>

Verbs which are transitive become factitive par excellence. This means that the factitive of such verbs expresses the idea of letting act or ordering to act.
<tbl>Intransitive|Transitive;;
<uig rom="ungsi-">ᠤᠩᠰᠢ ᠎</uig>  to read|<uig rom="ungsiγul-">ᠤᠩᠰᠢᠭᠤᠯ ᠎</uig>  to order to read;;
<uig rom="bici-">ᠪᠢᠴᠢ ᠎</uig>  to write|<uig rom="bicigül-">ᠪᠢᠴᠢᠭᠦᠯ ᠎</uig>  to let write</tbl>
